  "content_description": "Action Item - Teams",
  "content_text_body": "The goal is for each team member to build some simple habits to improve decision making processes on the team.\n\n### Restate the reasons\n\nWhen communicating a decision to your team or manager, start by reminding everyone what the decision is intended to achieve. Why are you prioritizing these particular goals at this time? Why did you choose this approach?\n\n### Reflect on your process\n\nReflect on how you made the decision. What sources of information were used (e.g., stakeholder input, data)? Who were the backers and approvers of the decision? Who else contributed to it? What external opinions were sought? How long did it take? Why are you prioritizing these particular goals at this time? \n\n### Be flexible and adjust\n\nMake sure you are clear about the assumptions and educated guesses you made while making your decision. Let your team know which parts of your decision you are confident about and which parts would benefit from more team input. Be sure to monitor and adjust goals as priorities change, and discuss any changes that affect other team members.",
